1. DEFINITIONS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 "Cache Networks" means the copyright owner or owners publishing CDNPanel
under the Cache Networks name, together with any successor that lawfully
acquires the relevant rights.

1.2 "CDNPanel" means the software project distributed from the official
repository currently located at:

    https://github.com/cachenetworks/CDNPanel

and any official successor repository designated by Cache Networks.

1.3 "Software" means all copyrightable material made available as part of
CDNPanel by Cache Networks, including source code, scripts, configuration,
database schemas, migrations, build files, Docker files, user-interface code,
documentation, examples, tests, templates, project-specific assets, and other
repository content, except Third-Party Material as defined below.

1.4 "Official Repository" means the CDNPanel repository controlled by Cache
Networks and any successor repository explicitly designated by Cache Networks.

1.5 "You" or "Your" means the individual or legal person exercising rights
under this License.

1.6 "Personal Use" means use by a natural person primarily for private,
non-commercial purposes and not on behalf of a business, employer, customer,
client, commercial operation, paid community, organisation, or other third
party.

1.7 "Commercial Use" means use primarily intended for commercial advantage,
financial compensation, revenue generation, cost recovery from third parties,
business operations, resale, paid hosting, paid support, paid access,
subscription services, advertising-supported services, or another activity
connected with trade or commerce.

1.8 "Organisational Use" means use by or for a company, partnership,
association, incorporated or unincorporated organisation, government body,
educational institution, club, paid community, employer, client, customer, or
other group, whether or not the organisation is operated for profit.

1.9 "Community Fork" means a GitHub fork of the Official Repository maintained
primarily for bona fide contribution, review, testing, issue reproduction,
discussion, or development work intended to benefit CDNPanel or assist the
CDNPanel community.

1.10 "Modification" means any alteration, adaptation, translation, port,
refactor, extension, deletion, rearrangement, or other change to the Software.

1.11 "Derivative Work" means a work based upon or incorporating copyrightable
expression from the Software to the extent recognised by applicable law.

1.12 "Covered Excerpt" means source code or other copyrightable expression
copied or adapted from the Software, including one or more non-trivial lines,
functions, classes, components, schemas, configuration blocks, documentation
passages, or other identifiable expression. A purely functional idea, fact,
algorithmic concept, public API concept, short name, or independently created
expression is not automatically a Covered Excerpt merely because it resembles
the Software.

1.13 "Redistribution" means making the Software, a Modification, a Derivative
Work, or a substantial or identifiable portion of it available to another
person by any means, including publication, release, upload, mirror,
repository, archive, package registry, container registry, download site,
bundle, binary distribution, source distribution, or transfer.

1.14 "Hosted Service" means making the Software or a Modification available for
third-party use over a network, including software-as-a-service (SaaS),
platform-as-a-service, managed hosting, managed CDN services, hosted control
panels, hosted APIs, commercial demonstrations, or other remotely accessible
services.

1.15 "Contribution" means code, documentation, tests, designs, patches,
configuration, examples, or other copyrightable material intentionally
submitted to Cache Networks for possible inclusion in CDNPanel.

1.16 "Third-Party Material" means material included in, used by, linked from, or
distributed with the Software that is owned by someone other than Cache
Networks and is governed by a separate license or terms.

