4. COMMUNITY FORKS EXPRESSLY PERMITTED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 Cache Networks expressly permits Community Forks on GitHub for genuine
community-development purposes.

4.2 Permitted Community Fork activities include:

a. preparing bug fixes;
b. preparing features and enhancements;
c. refactoring code;
d. improving performance or reliability;
e. adding or improving tests;
f. improving documentation;
g. reproducing bugs;
h. investigating reported issues;
i. conducting code review;
j. demonstrating proposed changes;
k. collaborating with other CDNPanel contributors;
l. submitting pull requests;
m. maintaining an in-progress branch for a proposed contribution; and
n. other good-faith development activity intended to improve CDNPanel.

4.3 A Community Fork may be public where GitHub's normal fork workflow makes
the fork public.

4.4 Every Community Fork must:

a. remain linked to or clearly identify the Official Repository as its origin;
b. retain this LICENSE file in full;
c. retain existing copyright and attribution notices;
d. clearly state that it is an unofficial development fork if there is any
   reasonable possibility of confusion;
e. avoid branding that suggests endorsement or official status unless Cache
   Networks has given written permission;
f. be used primarily for contribution, review, testing, discussion, or related
   community-development purposes; and
g. comply with every other restriction in this License.

4.5 A Community Fork must NOT be used to:

a. launch an independent CDNPanel distribution;
b. publish independent releases for end users;
c. operate a competing project;
d. create a rebranded CDNPanel product;
e. sell or monetise CDNPanel;
f. operate a Hosted Service for third parties;
g. publish prebuilt binaries, packages, or container images as an independent
   distribution;
h. create a general-purpose mirror or alternative download source;
i. remove or weaken this License; or
j. evade any restriction of this License.

4.6 The Community Fork permission is an exception to the general
Redistribution restriction only to the minimum extent reasonably necessary for
GitHub-based contribution and community review.

