10. HOSTED SERVICES AND NETWORK ACCESS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

10.1 You may run CDNPanel for Personal Use, including operating a personal,
non-commercial instance that delivers files belonging to or controlled by You.

10.2 Public visitors retrieving files from Your own personal, non-commercial
project does not, by itself, turn that deployment into a prohibited Hosted
Service, provided You are not providing third parties with CDNPanel accounts,
tenants, storage allocations, upload capability, API access, administrative
access, managed CDN services, or a comparable service offering.

10.3 You may not offer CDNPanel, a Modification, or a substantially similar
Derivative Work as a Hosted Service for third parties without written
permission.

10.4 Prohibited Hosted Service activity includes providing accounts, tenants,
API keys, storage allocations, uploads, file-management functionality,
administration, managed CDN functionality, or other CDNPanel service features
to customers, clients, organisations, or the general public.

10.5 A temporary development deployment reasonably necessary to demonstrate a
Contribution to Cache Networks is permitted where access is limited to project
reviewers and the deployment is not marketed, monetised, or operated as an
independent service.

